    64	* **full-field contract** (C2 timing, the contract of the P1/qualify ROM timings: "full-field input sampled at quadrature
    65	  points; full-field decode"): the six fields on the $(N+1)^2$ nodes of the ROM mesh $N$. FD with $L=N$: native; $L>N$
    66	  ($N\mid L$): restriction by stride; $L<N$ ($L\mid N$): the same sine interpolation to mesh $N$. PS: sine synthesis on
    67	  mesh $N$ (pscore's `sine_synth_last` on zero-padded coefficients).
    68	
    69	Lattice-contract fields of a full-field run are its stride-$N/256$ restriction, so the two contracts give **identical
    70	lattice errors** (checked, gate G-CT). The ROM's input is its full-field IC on mesh $N$ sampled at its quadrature points
    71	inside the timed query (P1 contract, unchanged); each FOM's input preparation is timed separately and reported, never
    72	added to a ratio (speed3d A2.7(e)).
    73	
    74	## 3. C1 — the FOM ladder
    75	
    76	| family | mesh / modes | $\Delta t$ | tolerance levels |
    77	|---|---|---|---|
    78	| F-CC | $L\in\{64,128,256,512,1024,2048,4096\}$ | $\{0.025,0.0125,0.01,0.005,0.0025\}$ | calibrated (below) |
    79	| F-UB | $L\in\{128,256,512,1024,2048,4096\}$ | $\{0.005,0.0025,0.00125,0.000625\}$ | calibrated |
    80	| F-PS | $N\in\{16,24,32,48,64,96,128,192,256\}$ | $\{0.025,0.0125,0.01,0.005,0.0025,0.001,0.0005\}$ | none (explicit) |
    81	
    82	That is 35 + 24 + 63 = 122 configurations, each run on all 38 cases (lattice contract).
    83	
    84	**Tolerance levels (FD):** $t_0=(10^{-10},10^{-11})$ (reference), $t_1=(10^{-8},10^{-9})$, $t_2=(10^{-6},10^{-7})$,
    85	$t_3=(10^{-4},10^{-5})$ as $(n_{\rm tol},l_{\rm tol})$. **Calibration** per (family, $L$, $\Delta t$) on dev6 cases 0–3:
    86	$t_0$ must pass (finite; every stage's recorded relative residual $\le n_{\rm tol}$; complete stage evidence; a stage
    87	that stops at the 20-iteration limit with the residual met counts as converged and is flagged — speed3d A2.5/A4.2), else
    88	the configuration is **unavailable** (no fallback). The chosen level is the **loosest** $t_\ell$ that passes the same
    89	convergence test and whose lattice output differs from $t_0$'s by $\le10^{-6}\,n_0$ at every output time on all four
    90	cases ($n_0=\lVert R(t_0)\rVert$). Production then runs all 38 cases at the chosen level; a production case with any
    91	unconverged stage makes the configuration **inadmissible** (reported, never matched).
    92	
    93	**PS validity:** finite outputs and finite running $\max|u|$ on every case; otherwise inadmissible (explicit
    94	ETDRK4 at large $\Delta t$ is expected to blow up at small viscosity — reported).
    95	
    96	**Screening cost:** per configuration, after its 38 production runs, the warm lattice-contract time on dev6 cases 0, 1
    97	× 3 repetitions (output hash equal to the production run), median. Screening costs only **order** candidates; every
    98	cost that enters a speed-up comes from a C2 paired panel (§5).
    99	
   100	**Per-family FOM Pareto front (C1 deliverable):** admissible configurations not beaten in all of screening cost,
   101	median error and worst error (descriptive), with cost per FOM at each mesh.
   102	
   103	## 4. Selection (matching) rules — pre-declared
   104	
   105	For a **target** $T$ (a ROM front member at mesh $N$, with its per-case E0 errors) and a family $f$:
   106	
   107	* **Admissible** FOM configuration: calibrated (FD) / valid (PS); converged and finite with complete evidence on every
   108	  one of the 38 cases; finite scores; hash-checked finite screening timings.
   109	* **Common population:** the cases of $T$'s published population that are E0-eligible; $\eta$ must agree between the
   110	  ROM's and the FOM's score records (same store version) to $10^{-15}$.
   111	* **Joint match (primary):** median **and** worst tie-or-beat $T$'s (§1 rule). **Median-only match** and **worst-only
   112	  match** are recorded too (brief: "record both median-matched and worst-matched comparisons").
   113	* **Selection:** the screening-cheapest matching configuration. **Confirmation by paired timing:** the three
   114	  screening-cheapest joint matches (fewer if fewer exist) are all timed in the C2 panel; the confirmed comparator is the
   115	  one with the smallest paired cost among them. Median-only and worst-only selections are timed (top 1 each).
   116	* **Same-mesh match** (crossover (a)), FD families only: the screening-cheapest joint match among configurations with
   117	  $L=N$. If none matches, "no same-mesh match"; the most accurate (lowest worst error) admissible configuration at
   118	  $L=N$ is then timed and reported as an **unmatched** same-mesh comparison with both errors beside. PS has no mesh in
   119	  this sense and enters only (b) and the union.
   120	* **Labels.** Every matched speed-up is an **upper bound on the claimed ROM speed-up** (a finite ladder gives an upper
   121	  bound on the optimal FOM cost; V4-6, speed3d `DESIGN.md:373–379`). A match at a **ladder edge** (the family's coarsest
   122	  mesh / fewest modes, or its largest $\Delta t$) is flagged "edge": a cheaper FOM outside the ladder might also match.
   123	  "No ladder match" = no admissible member ties-or-beats jointly; nothing is claimed for that cell.
   124	* Matched labels **never transfer across ROM meshes**: matching is recomputed against the ROM's errors at each mesh.
   125	
   126	Before FRONT-2D exists, the same matcher is run against P1's 22 qualified configurations as a **preview** (labelled
   127	"preview against P1 configurations; superseded by FRONT-2D"; it selects nothing).
   128	
   129	## 5. C2 — paired timing and crossover
   130	
   131	**One job per ROM mesh $N\in\{256,1024,4096\}$, all on H200** (the 4096² bank needs 68.7 GB, P1). In each job:
   132	
   133	* **A** (common baseline) = the P1 reference ROM configuration at mesh $N$: R384, gauss128, frozen mode list, LSPG-CN-R
   134	  at $\Delta t_0$, **fused full query** (init + evolve + decode), full-field contract.
   135	* **Subjects B:** every FRONT-2D member at mesh $N$ (fused full query, full-field contract) and every FOM selected in §4
   136	  for any of them (full-field contract, one jitted call). Duplicates timed once.
   137	* **Untimed scoring run** of every subject on the timing cases first: ROM per-case errors must reproduce FRONT-2D's to
   138	  $|\Delta e|\le10^{-9}$ (gate G-RR); FOM per-case errors must reproduce the ladder's to $|\Delta e|\le10^{-9}$ (G-FR).
   139	  Every later timed call's output must equal its scoring run's (identity: bitwise sha256; if the smoke shows that a
   140	  family is not bitwise reproducible on the GPU, the pre-declared fallback is max relative difference $\le10^{-12}$, stated
   141	  per family).
   142	* **Triplets:** dev6 cases × 3 repetitions, randomised order (seeded), each `burn | A | burn | B | burn | A`, warm JIT
   143	  (every subject run once per case before timing), drift $t_{A2}/t_{A1}\in[1/1.1,1.1]$ else repeated (≤ 2 retries) else
   144	  invalid; P1's `timing.panel_validity` subject-level rule.
   145	* **Cost** of B: median over valid (case, rep) of $t_B/\tfrac12(t_{A1}+t_{A2})$; absolute seconds beside. **Speed-up** of ROM
   146	  $X$ against FOM $Y$: $S={\rm cost}(Y)/{\rm cost}(X)$. **Interval:** 10,000 case-level bootstrap resamples (cases with
   147	  replacement; per case the median ratio over repetitions), percentile 95 %. With six cases the interval is coarse;
   148	  "inconclusive" is an expected outcome.
   149	
   150	**Crossover (a) same-mesh**, per FD family and front member: $S_a(N)$ against the same-mesh comparator at each $N$.
   151	**Crossover (b) best matched**, per family and the **union** (the cheapest confirmed joint match over the three
   152	families): $S_b(N)$. A crossover is reported only as a **bracket between actually run meshes** ("ROM faster from $N_i$",
   153	"between $N_i$ and $N_{i+1}$", "not reached by $4096^2$", "ROM faster at every mesh") using the interval rule: ROM
   154	faster at $N$ iff the lower bound of $S\ge1$; FOM faster iff the upper bound $<1$; else unresolved. Never interpolated
   155	(governing plan E4: speed-ups are read from actually run settings). The same bracket is reported for $S\ge2$.
   156	
   157	**H-comp (2D) decision rule (V3-5):** per (front member, family) cell and for the union, at $4096^2$ and at $1024^2$:
   158	**pass** ("≥ 2× faster at matched accuracy") iff joint-matched and the lower bound of $S_b\ge2$; **fail** iff the upper
   159	bound $<2$; **inconclusive** otherwise; "no ladder match" cells claim nothing. "≥ 2×" is stated only for passing cells.
   160	**K2** (governing plan): fires iff, at $4096^2$, every linear-span front member's union speed-up has upper bound $<2$;
   161	does not fire iff some member passes; otherwise inconclusive. If it fires it is reported prominently, as a valid result.
   162	
   163	## 6. Gates (must pass) and controls (must fail), each checked on real data in the cluster smoke
   164	
   165	| id | kind | check | blocks |
   166	|---|---|---|---|
   167	| G-FD1 | gate | lane `fomcore2` equals E0 `refcore` bit-for-bit (CPU, $L=256$, dev6 case 0, central CN-R and upwind BE) | every FD number |
