   169	| G-E0 | gate (**reproduce a trusted FOM**) | F-CC at $L=2048$, $\Delta t=0.00125$, $(10^{-11},10^{-9})$ on dev6 cases 0, 1 equals the stored E0 level `a0_L2048` lattice fields to $10^{-10}$ relative (GPU) | every F-CC number |
   170	| G-PS1 | gate | `psjax2d` lattice output equals `pscore.make_ps(N,2).run` to $10^{-12}$ relative ($N=32$, 2 cases); control: half $\Delta t$ differs by $>10^{-9}$ | every F-PS number |
   171	| G-PS2 | gate (**reproduce a trusted FOM**) | F-PS reproduces one stored E0 cross-check PS field (val32 case 0, run `N1024_dt0_a0`: its stored $N$, $\Delta t$ and IC quadrature) to $10^{-10}$ relative | every F-PS number |
   172	| G-INT | gate | sine interpolation exact at coincident nodes ($10^{-14}$) and exact for a band-limited sine field ($10^{-12}$); PS FFT synthesis equals pscore matrix synthesis at the lattice ($10^{-12}$) | $L<256$ and full-field outputs |
   173	| G-CT | gate | lattice restriction of a full-field output equals the lattice-contract output to $10^{-13}$ (each family, $N=1024$) | C2 accuracy pairing |
   174	| K-loose | control | tolerance level X $=(10^{-2},10^{-3})$ with at most 1 Newton iteration at (F-CC, $L=256$, $\Delta t=0.01$) is **rejected** by calibration | calibration / "non-converged or too loose comparator rejected" |
   175	| K-syn | control | synthetic matcher entries (zero cost but one unconverged case; zero cost but errors $10e_{\rm ROM}+4\eta+10^{-3}$) are rejected for every target | every match |
   176	| K-false | control | a **falsely matched pair**: the selected real FOM's per-case errors with its worst case raised to $\max(e_T)+3\eta$ (median unchanged) must fail the joint match and pass the median-only match; and with every case raised by $3\eta$ above $T$'s median must fail the median match | every joint match |
   177	| K-swap | control | scoring a FOM field against another case's reference, or with output times shifted by one, changes the score by $>10^{-6}$ | every score |
   178	| T-dbl | control (positive) | B = A executed twice back-to-back in one timed interval: ratio in $[1.8,2.2]$ | every C2 ratio |
   179	| T-fault | control | an injected fault (one subject's $A_2$ interval contains A executed twice): its drift is outside the band and the triplet is invalid | the drift gate |
   180	| T-id | control | an injected wrong identity reference for one subject invalidates its triplets | identity veto |
