   230	reported beside. **TOST** = two one-sided Wilcoxon signed-rank tests (`scipy.stats.wilcoxon`, `zero_method='wilcox'`,
   231	`method='auto'`, i.e. exact for $n\le50$ without zeros/ties) of $d_i+1>0$ (`alternative='greater'`) and $d_i-1<0$
   232	(`'less'`), α = 0.05 each; equivalence iff both reject. Estimand label: "normalised signed-rank equivalence", not a test
   233	of the mean error difference. Within-margin fraction $=\#\{|d_i|\le1\}/n$ of the pair's population. Trend: per-case OLS
   234	slope of $e$ vs $\log_2N$ over the three meshes on the 16-case subset (three-mesh eligible intersection); two-sided
   235	Wilcoxon of the slopes vs 0, α = 0.05; zero slopes dropped; fewer than 6 non-zero slopes → "not testable".
   236	**Pass** = TOST equivalence for both pairs **and** within-margin ≥ 90 % in each pair's actual population.
   237	**Fail** = TOST fails for at least one pair **and** (trend rejects **or** < 50 % of some pair within margin).
